globalThis.pzCourseExport="# Magnesium oxide · course dossier\n\nRevision: Revision 66\ncourse:267ac6eb-8bc0-581a-b003-44a39448de92\ndocumented_course\n2026-02-26 · Reported end 2026-04-29 · Span from evidence of start/use to recorded stop, pause or depletion; individual days may have been skipped.\nDate-window anchor: Recorded course start · 2026-02-26\n\n## Baseline before the selected anchor\n\n- 2026-01-30 · Marked fall in tolerance for speech, posture and typing · During a cluster around SAG/glutathione and post-sexual flares he reported being mostly motionless in bed. Typing a phone message, sitting up or speaking a few words could immediately bring forearm fatigue, burning, nape sensations and forehead pressure. He could sometimes scroll or listen to a podcast. · previous ability to type slowly or watch videos for hours · Prior capacity and early onset are recalled; objective strength or a specific causal exposure was not measured. Some grip symptoms were already becoming milder.\n  Source · baseline_states:BL-24\n\n## Intended targets\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Actions and doses\n\n- 2026-02-26 · Restart · 400 mg\n  Source · 2026-02-26 · restart · 400 mg · inferred diary day · reported_use · primary · S2:5230–5230 · [intervention_events:S2-L05230-E2]\n- 2026-03-03 · Miss\n  Source · 2026-03-03 · miss · inferred diary day · omission_or_hold · primary · S2:5306–5306 · [intervention_events:S2-L05306-E1]\n- 2026-03-03 · Schedule · every other day\n  Source · 2026-03-03 · schedule · every other day · inferred diary day · reported_change · primary · S2:5306–5306 · [intervention_events:S2-L05306-E2]\n- 2026-03-05 · Decrease · 400 → 200 mg\n  Source · 2026-03-05 · decrease · 400 → 200 mg · inferred diary day · reported_change · primary · S2:5342–5342 · [intervention_events:S2-L05342-E1]\n- 2026-03-19 · Increase · 200 → 400 mg\n  Source · 2026-03-19 · increase · 200 → 400 mg · inferred diary day · reported_change · primary · S2:5576–5576 · [intervention_events:S2-L05576-E1]\n- 2026-04-29 · Ran out\n  Source · 2026-04-29 · ran_out · inferred diary day · omission_or_hold · primary · S2:6283–6283 · [intervention_events:S2-L06283-E1]\n\n## Course timing evidence\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Potential effects\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Potential effects reported outside a specific course\n\n- On October 2 the patient took double their usual magnesium oxide during severe constipation, then passed a substantial stool with residual lower abdominal discomfort. On October 4 a further bowel movement relieved pain. They separately questioned whether increased famotidine was helping. · patient report\n  Source · archive_findings:S1-F2-58031 | claim:5414a85a-6ec6-5d87-9cf1-1ed0db62c608 | entity · Magnesium oxide; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n\n## Source evidence and qualifications\n\n- [archive_messages:S1-M69366] · reported 2026-02-14T21:27:22+01:00 · I wasn't markedly worse today compared to yesterday interestingly Maybe it kicks in tomorrow or i get away with it That said my baseline is abysmal almost no exertion tolerance, lying in bed mostly motionless all day · patient message · 2026-02-14T21:27:22+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M69556] · reported 2026-02-15T22:39:03+01:00 · description of this new type of PEM that has started appearing post-bezisterim and became really strong after the glutathione/SAG and then orgasm induced crash loop the starkest difference is in exertion capacity; before i could spend a few hours at a time typing slowly and watching videos etc on laptop, with only some mild peripheral tingling and neuro symptoms fluctuating. the only really bad pem i’d only get post-sexual exertion, the so called “poisoned pem” now baseline is lying in bed almost motionless or sometimes scrolling or listening to a podcast. if i start being more active, eg typing message on phone, sitting up, speaking a few words, immediate pem/pese follows as described below 1. starts with a mild surface level burn and a bit of fatigue in upper wrists and lower part of upper forearms (never the bottom side of arm muscles). it gets harder to hold onto phone, to keep arms fixed at their current rotation point. so eg imagine i’m propped up against wall in bed, phone is planted on my belly and i’m holing with both hands. it becomes more difficult to keep the phone from falling over, as if it had a larger mass than it actually does. when this first started appearing my arms and gripping strength were much weaker, noticeably so, now it’s getting milder, suggesting i’m maybe coming out of this. 2. then forehead pressure and radiating sensations very strongly and suddenly kick in (between eyebrows mainly). this is what i called \"lactate brain\" initially, after bezi, when i only had this symptom without the rest. this progresses into the entire forehead, behind eyes, a bit of the scalp, etc getting engulfed in this new weird sensation that i had initially called lactate. stinging, slightly sharp burny, surface level, but diffuse, no clear pain points. 3. usually simultaneously with or soon after previous step: nape pulsing, discomfort and fatigue, sometimes a clamping pressure when things get bad, and always mild surface burning start. this is the hardest to pin down, please do ask clarifying quesitons. i tried to locate the exact source, it's around the base of the skull where the neck meets the skull, but it's not a specific muscle pain or even the hernia like pain i had once in lower back, more of a nondescript, diffuse mild burning radiation coming from deeper perhaps, as well as same kind of fatigue there i feel in wrists/forearms, but not brain stem level deep maybe. it would make the most sense, given that CCI i'd assume would be persistent and not just post-activity. also reminder that eg during eating i have no pain there, as eating does improve overall function almost always. 4. this “lactate brain” diffuse sensation from both sides of the skull radiate across the scalp or maybe the meninges, it’s again hard to say exactly where the sensation is. 5. overall deep malaise feeling, but different from the usual \"toxic sludge\" feeling (which is more acutely felt inside brain, spine and overall systemic) sitting up in bed and typing on phone most easily triggers this sequence, but such whole body movement doesn’t seem necessary, because e.g. when i was lying motionless and spoke a few words yesterday, the same symptom sequence started almost immediately (maybe less forearm fatigue? i can’t recall). given it's so reactive, i'm not sure it's classical PEM, though obviously is post-exertional and the fatigue which i’m not feeling for the first time seems obviously PEM-y. this particular flavor of PEM is completely new. unsure what it means. nerve damage? all three areas of pain have significant nerves running through them (median nerve in wrist, occipital nerves in neck, various trigeminal nerves in face/forehead). however, forearm weakness seems most definitely muscular fatigue. · patient account or question · 2026-02-15T22:39:03+01:00\n- [baseline_states:BL-24] · 2026-01-30 · through 2026-02-15 · Marked fall in tolerance for speech, posture and typing · During a cluster around SAG/glutathione and post-sexual flares he reported being mostly motionless in bed. Typing a phone message, sitting up or speaking a few words could immediately bring forearm fatigue, burning, nape sensations and forehead pressure. He could sometimes scroll or listen to a podcast. · previous ability to type slowly or watch videos for hours · Prior capacity and early onset are recalled; objective strength or a specific causal exposure was not measured. Some grip symptoms were already becoming milder.\n- [diary_logs:S2-L04742] · 2026-01-30 · 0- strange tingling/pulsing pemyness 5 eat rice beef veggies 5.20- evening pem, pusling tingling becoming more intense 6.30 sleep 12.30 wake 13-19 sinus pressure mild and strong eye sensation 15.30 eat rice beef veggies 15.30-16.40 constant typing, depression, despair, etc 16.40- pem, poisoned 20.45- sinus pressure stronger again, eye sensation too 21 eat rice beef veggies 22- pemy 23-2chat and type a lot 1.5 changes: stop SAG as it may have exacerbated sinus and poisoned pem symptoms 2- mild poisoned feeling, typed too much · inferred_from_clock_rollover\n- [intervention_events:S2-L05230-E2] · 2026-02-26 · reported 2026-02-26 · Magnesium oxide · restart · 400 mg · inferred diary day · reported_use · primary\n- [intervention_events:S2-L05306-E1] · 2026-03-03 · reported 2026-03-03 · Magnesium oxide · miss · inferred diary day · omission_or_hold · primary\n- [intervention_events:S2-L05306-E2] · 2026-03-03 · reported 2026-03-03 · Magnesium oxide · schedule · every other day · inferred diary day · reported_change · primary\n- [intervention_events:S2-L05342-E1] · 2026-03-05 · reported 2026-03-05 · Magnesium oxide · decrease · 400 → 200 mg · inferred diary day · reported_change · primary\n- [intervention_events:S2-L05576-E1] · 2026-03-19 · reported 2026-03-19 · Magnesium oxide · increase · 200 → 400 mg · inferred diary day · reported_change · primary\n- [intervention_events:S2-L06283-E1] · 2026-04-29 · reported 2026-04-29 · Magnesium oxide · ran_out · inferred diary day · omission_or_hold · primary\n- [source_lines:S2:4747] · 12.30 wake\n- [source_lines:S2:4748] · 13-19 sinus pressure mild and strong eye sensation\n- [source_lines:S2:4749] · 15.30 eat rice beef veggies\n- [source_lines:S2:4750] · 15.30-16.40 constant typing, depression, despair, etc\n- [source_lines:S2:4751] · 16.40- pem, poisoned\n- [source_lines:S2:4752] · 20.45- sinus pressure stronger again, eye sensation too\n- [source_lines:S2:4753] · 21 eat rice beef veggies\n- [source_lines:S2:4754] · 22- pemy\n- [source_lines:S2:4755] · 23-2chat and type a lot\n- [source_lines:S2:4757] · 1.5\n- [source_lines:S2:4758] · changes: stop SAG as it may have exacerbated sinus and poisoned pem symptoms\n- [source_lines:S2:5230] · changes try oral IMI + DMSO → mild allergic reaction; restart mg oxide 400mg (1 pack)\n- [source_lines:S2:6283] · Changes run out of mg oxide\n- [treatment_intervals:S2-I-S2-L05230-E2] · 2026-02-26 · through 2026-04-29 · Magnesium oxide · 2026-02-26 · 2026-04-29 · reported_endpoint · Span from evidence of start/use to recorded stop, pause or depletion; individual days may have been skipped. · primary";
